  "correctness": "All derived-key controls match the independently validated Tanh reference byte for byte. Repeated native Tanh artifacts and the native-only Tanh file match each other byte for byte; native Tanh is decoded independently once. GeLU and Sigmoid each receive fresh independent decoding.",
  "timing_scope": "The first Tanh trial is a warm-up and excluded from the means. Four measured trials use derived20/native44/native44/derived20 with all prior parallel scheduling settings fixed. No compiler, unit test or independent decoder ran during timed trials. The host and paper hardware remain unmatched.",
  "interpretation": "Direct native encryption avoids the public derivation noise that made primary40 fail. The validated native44/112-chunk profile reduces observed Tanh evaluation time by about 7% and greatly shortens automorphism setup by loading cached keys. It does not close the remaining performance gap.",
  "usage": "Run ckks_narrow_ll14_native_auto_setup once with the retained checkpoint directory and a native-key directory. Supply --native-auto-directory DIRECTORY to the replay; --native-auto-pair 1 runs the warmed comparison. Native-only replay does not load the packed-key argument, demonstrated using a nonexistent placeholder path.",
  "default_key_source": "derived20 (native keys require an explicit directory)",
  "paper_reproduction_claim": false,
  "gap_closed": false,
